@qiangxue not sure if my issue is related to this...
I have simple AR model "Category". Category can have sub-categories.
In short, my model looks like this:

```
/**
 * @property integer $id
 * @property integer $parent_id
 *
 * @property Category[] $subCategories
 */
class Category extends ActiveRecord
{
    /**
     * @return ActiveQuery
     */
    public function getSubCategories()
    {
        return $this->hasMany(Category::className(), ['parent_id' => 'id']);
    }
}
```

When I load a list of categories with "subCategories" - I get the same error.
Code:

```
$items = Category::find()->joinWith(['subCategories'])->all();
```

Error:

```
SQLSTATE[42000]: Syntax error or access violation: 1066 Not unique table/alias: 'category'
The SQL being executed was: SELECT* FROM `category` LEFT JOIN `category` ON `category`.`id` = `category`.`parent_id`
```

Is there a way to set alias for "join" part?

@qiangxue mine is working, yours - not.

```
// works:
->from(['category' => 'category cat'])

// fails (not changing SQL-query):
->from(['cat' => 'category'])
->from(['category cat' => 'category'])
```
